# Citation metadata, in the Citation File Format (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#   Netwise is a capstone deliverable. It will be cited in a report, and may
#   be shown to an examiner, an employer, or whoever picks the project up
#   next. GitHub renders this as a "Cite this repository" panel and generates
#   BibTeX and APA from it, so the citation people use is one we wrote rather
#   than one they assemble from a URL.
#
#   The authors field deliberately matches LICENSE and NOTICE: an entity,
#   "The Netwise Authors", not four named individuals. A citation records who
#   made the work, which for a capstone touches university IP policy and an
#   external client -- see issue #91. Naming us here would answer that
#   question quietly, in a metadata file, which is the wrong place to settle
#   it. NOTICE lists the four of us and what each owns.
#
#   If the university requires named authors in a citation, replace the single
#   entity entry below with four `- family-names: / given-names:` entries.
#   Nothing else in this file changes.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Netwise: offline analysis and plain-English explanation of network device configurations"
message: "If you reference this software, please cite it using this metadata."
type: software

authors:
  - name: "The Netwise Authors"

abstract: >-
  Netwise reads exported network device configuration files, identifies
  security misconfigurations in them, and explains those findings in plain
  English. It orchestrates Batfish to build an offline model of the network
  and a locally hosted language model to translate the resulting technical
  findings, so no configuration data leaves the machine. The tool is passive:
  it reads exported files and never connects to, scans, or modifies a live
  network. Findings distinguish between a check that ran and found nothing and
  a check that could not run at all, on the basis that conflating the two is
  how a security tool reports safety nobody verified.

keywords:
  - network security
  - configuration analysis
  - Batfish
  - firewall
  - access control list
  - misconfiguration detection
  - explainable security
  - local language model

repository-code: "https://github.com/ARSH871-bot/Netwise"
license: Apache-2.0

# Tracks the most recent tagged release. Update both fields together when a
# new tag is cut -- CONTRIBUTING section 5b covers the release convention.
version: 0.3.0
date-released: "2026-08-12"
